// Title: Path To Screensaver Binary Modified
// Sigma ID: 67a6c006-3fbe-46a7-9074-2ba3b82c3000
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Bartlomiej Czyz @bczyz1, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-11 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1546.002
// Description: Detects value modification of registry key containing path to binary used as screensaver.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate modification of screensaver
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1546.002/T1546.002.md
//   - https://www.welivesecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/08/eset-gazer.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_event_modify_screensaver_binary_path.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Control Panel\\Desktop\\SCRNSAVE.EXE" and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\explorer.exe")))
